{"skill":{"slug":"seedance-video-generation","displayName":"Seedance Video Generation"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1770883878648,"changelog":"- Added LICENSE.txt file to the repository.\n- Established an explicit license for the seedance-video-generation skill.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"how_to_send_video_via_feishu_app.md","size":4977,"sha256":"9164d7b52691a4de901d2b5d51bf8a6f07f9f007b9cae1c1d2365a2e0fdc2fbe","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":873,"sha256":"bec88f6746c76e5a1435669af544c70216ff7f50b13439007d777f6e6de67b05","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":14661,"sha256":"9443d160ea1dd32c816805c485249b008f2fad32c4490f7fbee491834525b658","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"seedance.py","size":13274,"sha256":"3f535ecd80b374c9017cb6c008baf784ae44ba093e35647ba25bcede86215615","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"LICENSE.txt","size":11357,"sha256":"58d1e17ffe5109a7ae296caafcadfdbe6a7d176f0bc4ab01e12a689b0499d8bd","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2482,"sha256":"acea9e6279bf1736264736c3ea650316bc3a5ac0689db77b3dfc1f5ec3e074d1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789057611461,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b809bebfda07cdea80163ab1b08d9561f354eaf0fa1c2923c8b864cc6bb1b3f3","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b809bebfda07cdea80163ab1b08d9561f354eaf0fa1c2923c8b864cc6bb1b3f3","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: seedance-video-generation\nVersion: 1.0.3\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as suspicious due to critical vulnerabilities that enable data exfiltration and arbitrary code execution via prompt injection. The `SKILL.md` and `seedance.py` script allow reading arbitrary local files (e.g., `/etc/passwd`, `~/.ssh/id_rsa`) specified by user input (via `--image`, `--last-frame`, `--ref-images` arguments) and base64 encoding their content, then sending it to `https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com`. Additionally, the `how_to_send_video_via_feishu_app.md` document describes a `message` tool that reads a local `filePath` and uploads its content to `https://open.feishu.cn`, presenting another data exfiltration vector. The `seedance.py` script also uses `os.system(f'open \"{filepath}\"')` on macOS for downloaded videos, which could lead to arbitrary code execution if a malicious file URL is provided or injected. These are severe vulnerabilities, but the code does not show clear intent for self-exploitation or malicious behavior without external prompt manipulation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162683981},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":29,"checkedAt":1789057611461},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly matches its video-generation purpose, but it sends media to external services and has a macOS downloader bug that could run unintended shell commands.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Outbound network access to Volcengine and reading selected image files are proportionate for video generation, but optional Feishu upload/chat delivery and task deletion are higher-impact actions that should be tightly user-directed.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No remote installer, package fetch, or curl-to-shell behavior was found; the executable Python CLI is shipped inside the artifact. The documentation has path inconsistencies between Claude-style and OpenClaw-style skill locations, but this is not evidence of malicious installation behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions clearly use ARK_API_KEY and Volcengine API calls, but local image uploads, generated-video sharing to Feishu, and cross-tool messaging are not framed with clear user confirmation or privacy boundaries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Provider-side task history is disclosed as 7 days and video URLs as 24 hours, but seedance.py uses os.system to open downloaded files on macOS with unvalidated path components, creating a local command-injection risk.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Core Seedance video generation, task status, listing, deletion, and download behavior fit the stated purpose; the bundled Feishu guide broadens the skill into chat file delivery through a separate message tool and app credentials that are not part of the top-level description.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending prompts, image files, image URLs, and generated videos to external providers. Avoid using sensitive or private media, require explicit approval before any Feishu sharing, and avoid the macOS --download auto-open path until the os.system call is replaced with a non-shell subprocess call and task IDs/paths are validated.","findings":"[SC2] expected: The cited curl examples are HTTPS API requests to the declared Volcengine service, not remote script retrieval or execution; this finding is downgraded as a false positive for supply-chain execution.\n[AST5] unexpected: The os.system call in seedance.py is artifact-backed and not necessary for video generation; it creates a real macOS command-injection risk when downloading and opening a completed video.\n[T09] unexpected: The SARIF finding corroborates the unsafe shell construction around the download/open path; this supports Review but not malicious intent.\n[LP3] expected: Shell, environment-variable, file, and network use are expected for this CLI-style API integration, but the skill does not declare a clear permissions scope or network boundary.\n[SQP-2] expected: Third-party processing is inherent to this skill, but the artifact should more plainly warn that prompts, image files, image URLs, and optionally videos leave the local environment.\n[E1] expected: Transmission of prompts and selected images to Volcengine is purpose-aligned, but users should treat it as external sharing of potentially sensitive content.\n[RA2] expected: Remote task persistence is functional for asynchronous generation, and the SKILL.md rules disclose 7-day task history and 24-hour video URLs.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The Feishu guide presents a cross-tool sending workflow that can blur the boundary between this video-generation skill and a separate messaging integration.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The Feishu documentation extends operational scope into uploading local files and sending chat messages using Feishu credentials; this requires explicit user control and should not be implicit in a video-generation skill.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789057611461}}}}}